Subject: [PATCH] avformat/rtsp: keep TLS redirects secure and authority scoped

Optional companion of WineDMO proposal 0031. The pinned RTSP code retains
lower_rtsp_proto=tls once selected, even when a server redirects to an
rtsp:// URL, yielding TLS with a plaintext control URI/default-port state.
Reject non-rtsps redirects before replacing the URL. Continue accepting
same-host and cross-host rtsps redirects with per-connection hostname checks.

Clear inherited credentials and cached Basic/Digest challenge state when
the secure URL authority changes (case-insensitive hostname, normalized
default port). Explicit destination userinfo is handled by the existing
parser on the next connection pass. Compare URLs, not the local host buffer
which getpeername may have replaced with a numeric address.

This does not alter unencrypted RTSP redirects, invent a reconnect loop or
log redirect targets. It is source/native-policy tested only, not a TLS
handshake/runtime claim. Apply after SE1 FFmpeg fixes, not to Wine, and
require this companion before enabling the new secure aliases.
---
diff --git a/libavformat/rtsp.c b/libavformat/rtsp.c
--- a/libavformat/rtsp.c
+++ b/libavformat/rtsp.c
@@ -2180,7 +2180,37 @@
     ff_rtsp_close_streams(s);
     ff_rtsp_close_connections(s);
     if (reply->status_code >=300 && reply->status_code < 400 && s->iformat) {
-        int ret = ff_format_check_set_url(s, reply->location);
+        int ret;
+        /* TLS control URLs must remain secure across redirects.  In particular,
+         * do not reinterpret a plaintext Location using the previous TLS socket
+         * mode and secure default port. A new TLS connection verifies its own
+         * hostname; same-host and cross-host secure redirects remain allowed. */
+        if (!strcmp(lower_rtsp_proto, "tls") &&
+            !av_strstart(reply->location, "rtsps://", NULL)) {
+            err = AVERROR(EINVAL);
+            goto fail2;
+        }
+        if (!strcmp(lower_rtsp_proto, "tls")) {
+            char old_host[1024], new_host[1024];
+            int old_port, new_port;
+
+            /* The local host buffer may already hold getpeername()'s numeric
+             * address. Compare URL authorities, not that transport detail. */
+            av_url_split(NULL, 0, NULL, 0, old_host, sizeof(old_host), &old_port,
+                         NULL, 0, s->url);
+            av_url_split(NULL, 0, NULL, 0, new_host, sizeof(new_host), &new_port,
+                         NULL, 0, reply->location);
+            if (old_port < 0) old_port = RTSPS_DEFAULT_PORT;
+            if (new_port < 0) new_port = RTSPS_DEFAULT_PORT;
+            if (av_strcasecmp(old_host, new_host) || old_port != new_port) {
+                /* TLS authenticates the new server, not permission to send it
+                 * another authority's credentials or cached Digest challenge.
+                 * Explicit destination userinfo is parsed on the next pass. */
+                memset(rt->auth, 0, sizeof(rt->auth));
+                memset(&rt->auth_state, 0, sizeof(rt->auth_state));
+            }
+        }
+        ret = ff_format_check_set_url(s, reply->location);
         if (ret < 0) {
             err = ret;
             goto fail2;
